! Silicon for an ultracell calculation: the two-atom cell, no symmetry, and an
! unshifted k-grid whose first dimension is a multiple of the ultracell length.
!
! Symmetry is off because a modulation breaks the crystal's point group and the
! ultracell's own group is not written; the grid is unshifted because the folded
! set k0 + Q is a Monkhorst-Pack grid only if its origin is.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.20,
    nat = 2, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 12.0,
    nosym = .true., noinv = .true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS automatic
 8 2 2 0 0 0
